(Retrieval Augmented Generation for Document Question Answering) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(NLP Lab Experiment Report) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(Abstract) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(This report documents a laboratory experiment that implements a Retrieval Augmented) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Generation \(RAG\) system. The system answers natural language questions using only the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(documents a user uploads, and every answer is accompanied by a citation pointing back to) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(the exact passage it was generated from.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The experiment covers the full pipeline: text extraction, cleaning, chunking, embedding) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(generation, vector storage, similarity retrieval and grounded answer generation.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(1. Objective) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The objective of the experiment is to build a question answering system that can answer) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(questions about a personal document collection without any prior fine-tuning of a) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(language model.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(A secondary objective is to verify that answers are grounded: the system must refuse to) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(answer when the retrieved context does not support an answer, rather than hallucinating) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(one.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The objective of the experiment is therefore twofold: demonstrate the mechanics of) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(retrieval augmented generation, and demonstrate that its outputs are traceable to their) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(sources.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(2. System Architecture) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The architecture has six stages. First the uploaded file is parsed into plain text. The) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(text is then cleaned to remove repeated page headers, fix hyphenation and normalise) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(whitespace.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The cleaned text is split into chunks of 500 characters with an overlap of 100) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(characters. The overlap exists so that a sentence straddling a chunk boundary is still) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(fully contained in one chunk.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Each chunk is encoded into a 384 dimensional vector. The vectors are stored in a) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(ChromaDB collection configured for cosine similarity.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(3. Embeddings) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The embedding model is sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2. It is a small bi-encoder) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(that maps a chunk of text into a dense vector of 384 dimensions, and it is chosen) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(because it is fast on CPU while still capturing semantic similarity well enough for) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(passage retrieval.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The same model embeds the user's question, which makes query and document vectors) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(directly comparable with a cosine similarity.) Tj
T*
T*
ET
endstream
