/F1 14 Tf
(9. Limitations) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(A limitation of the system is that retrieval quality depends heavily on the chunk size:) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(chunks that are too small lose context, while chunks that are too large dilute the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(signal and reduce precision.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Another limitation is that the system performs lexical and semantic matching only. It) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(cannot answer questions that require arithmetic over the documents, or reasoning that) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(spans many chunks at once.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Finally, scanned PDFs without a text layer cannot be processed because optical character) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(recognition is out of scope for this experiment.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf
(10. Conclusion) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The experiment demonstrates that a complete retrieval augmented generation workflow can) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(be built from standard open source components and run locally on a laptop CPU.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The key takeaways are that grounding depends on retrieval, that citations make the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(system auditable, and that abstaining is a feature rather than a failure when the corpus) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(does not cover the question.) Tj
T*
T*
ET
